  "claim": "Two independent registries, two ceremonies, two operators. The same receivable has the same pledge marker in both, because a marker is a function of the invoice and its parties alone. Asked before the second registry had ever seen the receivable, its own book answered FREE and only the peer answered ENCUMBERED, so the cross-registry question is what carried the information. The second registry then accepted the same receivable, because its ledger cannot see across and no contract can; the transaction showing that is recorded here. What stops the double pledge is the lender's check, which returns one bit per registry and nothing else.",
